{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-71915" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A function $p(t)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $t$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $p(t)$ | $3$ | $6$ | $9$ | $5$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n\nApproximate ${p}^{′}(t)$ at the point $t=0$ using a forward difference approximation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-71915" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{p}^{′}(t)≈\\frac{p(t+h)-p(t)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $t=0.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=1.$ This gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{′}(0) & ≈\\frac{p(0+1)-p(0)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{p(1)-p(0)}{1} \\\\  & =5-9 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-71915" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5d7ce2f639b79390f91ae6ef13ae0b13f19ceb5826a85548464a4ed1610ea55"} {"question" "q-71915" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-71915" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-71915" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-342003" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A function $d(y)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $y$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $d(y)$ | $-8.92$ | $-11.34$ | $-15.23$ | $-17.56$ | $-18.21$ | $-18.50$ |\n\nApproximate ${d}^{′}(y)$ at the point $y=-5$ using a forward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\n${d}^{′}(-5)≈$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-342003" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{d}^{′}(y)≈\\frac{d(y+h)-d(y)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $y=-5.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=2.$ This gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}^{′}(-5) & ≈\\frac{d(-5+2)-d(-5)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{d(-3)-d(-5)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-11.34-(-8.92)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2.42}{2} \\\\  & =-1.21.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-342003" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5d7ce2f639b79390f91ae6ef13ae0b13f19ceb5826a85548464a4ed1610ea55"} {"question" "q-342003" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-342003" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1.21"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-341994" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A function $g(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $0.3$ | $0.6$ | $0.9$ | $1.2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $-2.7$ | $-1.6$ | $-0.4$ | $1.1$ | $3.7$ |\n\nApproximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=0.6$ using a forward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\n${g}^{′}(0.6)≈$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-341994" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $x=0.6.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=0.3.$ This gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(0.6) & ≈\\frac{g(0.6+0.3)-g(0.6)}{0.3} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(0.9)-g(0.6)}{0.3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.1-(-0.4)}{0.3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.5}{0.3} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-341994" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5d7ce2f639b79390f91ae6ef13ae0b13f19ceb5826a85548464a4ed1610ea55"} {"question" "q-341994" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-341994" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-341996" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A function $g(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $20.4$ | $18.6$ | $16.5$ | $14.4$ | $12.3$ | $10.8$ |\n\nApproximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=2$ using a forward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\n${g}^{′}(2)≈$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-341996" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $x=2.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=2.$ This gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(2) & ≈\\frac{g(2+2)-g(2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(4)-g(2)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{14.4-16.5}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2.1}{2} \\\\  & =-1.05.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-341996" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5d7ce2f639b79390f91ae6ef13ae0b13f19ceb5826a85548464a4ed1610ea55"} {"question" "q-341996" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-341996" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1.05"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-71912" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A function $g(x)$ has values according to the table below:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $g(x)$ | $7.25$ | $8.5$ | $9.25$ | $5.75$ | $2.5$ |\n\nApproximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=3$ using a forward difference approximation." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-71912" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $x=3.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=1.$ This gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(3) & ≈\\frac{g(3+1)-g(3)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(4)-g(3)}{1} \\\\  & =2.5-5.75 \\\\  & =-3.25.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-71912" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5d7ce2f639b79390f91ae6ef13ae0b13f19ceb5826a85548464a4ed1610ea55"} {"question" "q-71912" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-71912" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1.75"] ["math" "-3.25"] ["math" "-4.25"] ["math" "1.25"] ["math" "2.5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-71912" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3.25"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-71921" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/assets/21e310adffbad6309176ea26549e0e43efe3d8e3d7f2f0b018902be16781802d.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=g(x)$ is shown above. Approximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=1.5$ using a forward difference approximation with step size $h=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-71921" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x)}{h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=1.5.$ Applying the above formula with $x=1.5$ and $h=1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(1.5) & ≈\\frac{g(1.5+1)-g(1.5)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(2.5)-g(1.5)}{1} \\\\  & =4-2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-71921" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f5d7ce2f639b79390f91ae6ef13ae0b13f19ceb5826a85548464a4ed1610ea55"} {"question" "q-71921" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-71921" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-71921" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-47386" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/assets/5f770f5be6b6131533dc23482281e82024737a4e5a61440dfe1baf5108786381.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $y=g(x)$ is shown above. \nApproximate ${g}^{′}(x)$ at the point $x=6$ using a forward difference approximation with step size $h=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-47386" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{g}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{g(x+h)-g(x)}{h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=6.$  Applying the above formula with $x=6$ and $h=4$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(6) & ≈\\frac{g(6+4)-g(6)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{g(10)-g(6)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{8-2}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{4} \\\\  & =1.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14057748/state.json" "file_sha256" "b1b53e298b7988267f7d0c5f1afaa4cc3e6ddc5d21133838fc130bd483344397"} {"question" "q-47386" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Develo